.TH strarray_to_argv 3
.SH NAME
strarray_to_argv \- convert string array to NULL-terminated argv
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "strarray.h"
.PP
.BI "char **strarray_to_argv(strarray *" arr ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B strarray_to_argv
converts the string array
.I arr
into a NULL-terminated array of strings suitable for use with functions like
.BR execve (2).
The caller is responsible for freeing the returned pointer array.